    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for owner creation. When more than 80 owners already carry today's (adjusted business-day) registration date at creation time, the new owner's `bulkSignupWarning` is `true`; otherwise `false`. The value is fixed at creation and returned unchanged on both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 consistent with the existing point-in-time fields like `namesakeCount`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only boolean `bulkSignupWarning` to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this at build time).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` persisted field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 set `bulkSignupWarning = countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate) > 80`, reusing the same daily-accumulation count the per-day limit rule uses (new `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant).\n- **`schema.sql`** for all four DB profiles (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column.\n\nMapStruct auto-maps the matching field name onto the DTO, so it flows through to the JSON response. The `coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` test (fresh create \u2192 `false`) and the whole suite are green.",
